# Pinned SHA-512 digests for the Debian cloud images the guest build starts from.
#
# This file is the trust anchor. Debian publishes SHA512SUMS for its cloud
# images but no detached signature for them, so the manifest served beside an
# image cannot be verified: whoever could serve a malicious qcow2 could serve a
# matching manifest next to it. A digest that only changes through a reviewed
# commit can not be substituted that way.
#
# The images are fetched from an immutable dated directory rather than the
# mutable "latest", so a rebuild from an old commit gets the same bytes.
#
# Format is `sha512sum -c` compatible: <digest>  <filename>
#
# To move to a newer Debian build:
#   1. Pick a directory from https://cloud.debian.org/images/cloud/trixie/
#   2. Take the digests from its SHA512SUMS — never from the image itself.
#   3. Update debianStamp in source.go to match, in the same commit.
